question_text:
The following change is made to `objstore.go` in the `thanos-io/objstore` repository:

```go
// Before
type Bucket interface {
	io.Closer
	BucketReader
	// Provider returns the providers of the underlying bucket.
	Provider() ObjProvider
	// Upload the contents of the reader as an object into the bucket.
	Upload(ctx context.Context, name string, r io.Reader) error
	// Delete removes the object with the given name.
	Delete(ctx context.Context, name string) error
	// Name returns the bucket name for the provider.
	Name() string
}

// After
type Bucket interface {
	io.Closer
	BucketReader
	// Provider returns the providers of the underlying bucket.
	Provider() ObjProvider
	// Upload the contents of the reader as an object into the bucket.
	Upload(ctx context.Context, name string, r io.Reader) error
	// Delete removes the object with the given name.
	Delete(ctx context.Context, name string) error
	// Name returns the bucket name for the provider.
	Name() string
	// Tags returns the metadata tags associated with the bucket.
	Tags(ctx context.Context) (map[string]string, error)
}
```

The `thanos-io/objstore` module is vendored by both `grafana/mimir` and `grafana/loki`. Every concrete type that satisfies `objstore.Bucket` must now also implement `Tags(ctx context.Context) (map[string]string, error)`. No other files are changed.

Which files across the repositories `grafana/mimir` and `grafana/loki` would fail to compile as a result of this change? List each file by its path relative to its repository root, and indicate which repository it belongs to.
